      "notes": "Measured 2026-08-16: the \"Ultima\" pagination link declares 7,451 pages at six rows, and page 7451 was fetched and found full at six -> 44,706 cases. That is a portal_count denominator in the sense this file requires, not a maximum identifier range. The registry is append-ordered, so the total grows; a shortfall against it means the sweep stopped early, not that the corpus shrank.\nGrain is `claim`, not `payment`: Cuant\u00eda Reclamada is an amount demanded and most rows never become a disbursement. Cantidad Adjudicada is the awarded figure where one exists, and is blank on unresolved cases \u2014 it must not be read as money paid.\nuniqueness_key is the surrogate rdc_case_uid rather than N\u00fam del Caso, which is not unique across the corpus. Coverage is counted over the list sweep; detail enrichment (scripts/enrich_rdc_details.py) fills the party fields incrementally and is deliberately not part of this denominator."
